  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resilient Women , Resilient Communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Strengthen women&apos;s economic empowerment and household resilience.
- Improve children&apos;s access to food, education and health through stable livelihoods.
- Increase climate adaptation in small scale activities.
- Build sustainable organisational capacity of a local NGO to operate independently and attract diversified funding.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project strengthens  economic resilience among vulnerable women-led households in Eastern Uganda through the climate adapted livelihoods, while simultaneously building long-term organisational capacity of a local Civil organisation. The intervention combines direct household-level livelihood support, community-based learning and dissemination, and structured organisational development focused on results management, reporting, fundraising and accountability.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project targets the disadvantaged community women especially but not limited to vulnerable single women who are also heads of households.</narrative>
  </description>
